1
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:12,080
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,120
=Episode 13=

3
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,720
(He Lan)

4
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,240
(Xiyu,)

5
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,600
(pick up.)

6
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,560
Keep an eye on him.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,760
(Swan Lake Principal Dancer: Luo Xiyu)
I'm outside now.

8
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:33,960
Where are you?

9
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,840
Why can't I see you?

10
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:20,440
He Lan!

11
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,000
He Lan!

12
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,600
(I got He Lan killed too.)

13
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:47,800
(He Lan...)

14
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,200
(Where's He Lan?)

15
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:53,800
He Lan!

16
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,440
He Lan!

17
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:55,200
It's me!

18
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,240
He Lan!

19
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,520
Why is he so cold?

20
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,400
There's not a trace of feeling
for me in his eyes.

21
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,240
Could it be because in the last loop,

22
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,600
he died protecting me?

23
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,280
And that

24
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,120
triggered a butterfly effect?

25
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,080
Did it break our ship bond?

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,200
(Is he no longer my destined love?)

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,200
I gave you a slice of strawberry cake
a month ago.

28
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,080
Remember?

29
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:44,960
Thanks.

30
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,200
That's...

31
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:47,800
That's it?

32
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,040
I'm Luo Xiyu.

33
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,600
You like me. Did you forget?

34
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:59,640
Luo Xiyu,

35
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,120
you're a girl.

36
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,640
Have some self-respect.

37
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,000
Xiaoba.

38
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:20,760
I need you to help me figure
something out.

39
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:23,560
So, I've...

40
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,120
been reading this novel lately.

41
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,720
The leads have been lovers
through several lifetimes.

42
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,040
In every life, the guy is madly
in love with her.

43
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:34,440
But in one lifetime,

44
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,520
he dies

45
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,000
saving her.

46
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,240
When she's given another chance
in life again,

47
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,440
he's completely different.

48
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,800
It's like he doesn't like her
at all anymore.

49
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Why do you think that is?

50
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,640
Why?

51
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,640
How would I know?
Wait for the novel's update.

52
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,360
But it's not updating!

53
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,360
I'm dying to know.

54
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:54,000
I'm scared it'll end tragically
or just fizzle out.

55
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,480
Could it be

56
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,840
that the guy

57
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,040
time-traveled too?

58
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,160
But he realized that being with her

59
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,200
only brings him bad luck,

60
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,200
so he's avoiding her on purpose?

61
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,080
No way.

62
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,480
That makes zero sense.

63
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:08,440
He was crazy in love with her
in his previous life,

64
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,400
and bam, he died.

65
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,920
Then he wakes up
with a second chance in life too?

66
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,640
They'd obviously fall into
each other's arms crying!

67
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:13,400
Why would he go,

68
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,560
"That girl's bad luck.

69
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,760
I better stay away from her"?

70
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,480
Then was all that love fake?

71
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,400
Absolutely not.

72
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:19,760
Go on.

73
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,400
Then...

74
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,680
could it be
because in the previous life,

75
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,920
the male lead died,

76
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,600
so his bond with the female lead

77
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:27,520
was severed?

78
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:28,680
It's possible.

79
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,720
That depends on whether there's

80
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,480
a strong second male lead.

81
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,960
There is,

82
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,520
but she doesn't like him.

83
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:38,720
From my many years
of reading romance novels,

84
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,480
canon couples like that

85
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,920
usually have some kind of invisible

86
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,600
bond.

87
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:47,480
(Wait.)

88
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:49,040
(We do!)

89
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:51,000
(When I grabbed his hand just now,)

90
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,480
(I definitely felt
a jolt of electricity.)

91
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:55,440
(And that family ring of his
just happens to recharge me.)

92
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,960
(Doesn't that prove we're canon?)

93
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,360
What does that mean?

94
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,880
(Academic Building)

95
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:31,480
We're doing an inspection now.

96
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,600
Everyone, line up outside.

97
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:57,840
What are you doing?

98
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,640
You look like an addict getting a fix.

99
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,680
You wouldn't understand.

100
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,320
I'm feeling the love.

101
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,480
There's still some time
before the Dance Academy exam.

102
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,280
I'm sure you'll recover by then.

103
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:12,200
What's wrong?

104
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,640
Are you feeling sick?

105
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,160
Uh,

106
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:14,760
no.

107
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:15,960
I think

108
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,080
I just pulled something in my neck.

109
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,560
Where do you think you're going?

110
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:23,480
Call the police!

111
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,560
Finally. I've been waiting for you guys.

112
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,520
You guys?

113
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:29,720
Oh,

114
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:30,960
I mean...

115
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,560
This is a public place,

116
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,680
and you dare pull a knife?

117
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,600
You little

118
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,280
street punks.

119
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,120
Don't think a knife
is enough to scare us.

120
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,240
In a minute, you'll be beaten senseless

121
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,160
and begging on your knees.

122
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:42,160
(Stay calm.)

123
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,800
(He Lan will be here any second.)

124
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,200
(He definitely still loves me.)

125
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,040
(He Lan has to be my match.)

126
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,160
Shut up, witch.

127
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,600
Keep yapping, and I'll slash
your pretty boy.

128
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,440
He's here!

129
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,240
You're not going to save us?

130
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:01,880
What's it got to do with me?

131
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:02,560
Wait.

132
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:03,560
He Lan!

133
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,120
Get them!

134
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,640
Don't go!

135
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,400
Run!

136
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,160
Run!

137
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,040
Why didn't you save me?

138
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,760
Why would I?

139
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:23,560
(This isn't how it goes
in romance dramas.)

140
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,440
(Even when the guy loses his memory,)

141
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,040
(he still loves her instinctively.)

142
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:30,160
(I just haven't triggered
his protective instincts yet.)

143
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,160
(No way will he stay this cold.)

144
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,560
(Men's Restroom)

145
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,920
(Now you'll finally come to my rescue,
right?)

146
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:47,680
(Our relationship will finally
get back on track.)

147
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,320
I hit my head.

148
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,200
I need help, now.

149
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,520
Help me up.

150
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,000
I need to go to the campus clinic.

151
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:01,600
You...

152
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,720
Come help me up.

153
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,400
(Billiards Club
Where Friends Meet Over a Game)

154
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:20,880
Watch out!

155
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,120
I'm He Lan's girlfriend.

156
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,160
If you've got a problem, come at me!

157
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:36,800
♪I orbit your planet as I sail♪

158
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:42,200
♪The world has never been this quiet♪

159
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,160
Watch out!

160
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:49,920
I'm He Lan's girlfriend.

161
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,400
If you've got a problem, come at me!

162
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:52,920
Get him!

163
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,160
Didn't you hear me?

164
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,480
I'm He Lan's girlfriend.

165
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,960
If you want someone, come at me!

166
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,600
(He Lan, hurry! Save me!)

167
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,600
(He's going to kill me! Hurry!)

168
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:10,560
What are you, lovesick?

169
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,440
Stay out of men's business.

170
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:13,760
Now get lost!

171
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,920
(Our bond really is over.)

172
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,800
(He Lan won't be with me in this life.)

173
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,440
(Then Wang Haotian won't hurt me)

174
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,920
(to get revenge on him.)

175
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,720
(I guess I can survive now.)

176
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,520
(Welcome to Xintiandi Billiards Club)

177
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:30,360
(But...)

178
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,960
(JUS)
(how come I'm not happy about it?)

179
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,840
(He Lan and I used to have
so many points of intersection.)

180
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:39,400
(But in this life,)

181
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:42,040
(we're destined to be two parallel lines
that never cross.)

182
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,040
You know,

183
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:44,840
people used to tell me

184
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,360
how hard it is to be a stepmother.

185
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,400
I never believed them.

186
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,480
But once you become one,

187
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,320
you realize how difficult it really is.

188
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,200
He Lan

189
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,600
isn't my biological son,

190
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,800
but after I married his father,

191
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,920
we brought He Lan

192
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,040
to live with us.

193
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,160
And what does he do?

194
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,240
He's either fighting

195
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:58,960
or spending every day

196
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,960
wasting his time at that billiards hall.

197
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,920
But He Lan gets great grades.

198
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,880
Maybe he'll make something of himself
and take care of you someday.

199
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:05,920
What good are grades?

200
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,760
He still got expelled.

201
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,000
Expelled?

202
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:09,960
That serious?

203
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,400
He did.

204
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,800
He stole something.

205
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:13,840
I'm telling you,

206
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,720
he hurt another student

207
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,800
so badly

208
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,600
that the boy spent

209
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,960
more than two weeks in the hospital.

210
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,560
How could the school keep him
after that?

211
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:21,400
Ma'am,

212
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,080
is what you just said actually true?

213
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,800
Wasn't it your son, Li Junsheng,

214
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,680
who wore He Lan's school jacket
when he went stealing

215
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,880
and got Wang Haotian hurt?

216
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,320
Li Junsheng framed He Lan,

217
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:32,160
and He Lan got expelled because of it.

218
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,000
And that's not all.

219
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,920
The money He Lan's grandma left him

220
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,160
was taken by you too.

221
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,600
And now you're badmouthing him
to the neighbors,

222
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,720
acting like being his stepmother
is such a burden.

223
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,760
What are you trying to do?

224
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,360
Who are you? What nonsense are you
talking about?

225
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:43,240
He Lan!

226
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,200
Who is she?

227
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,280
You've been trouble
since you were little,

228
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,400
and now you're dating too?

229
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,360
Mom, who are you arguing with?

230
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,760
I don't know her either.

231
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:50,880
I think she's He Lan's classmate.

232
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:51,920
Look, they're both running off.

233
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,320
Those little brats!

234
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:01,480
Wait.

235
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,600
Wait!

236
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,720
What are you doing?

237
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,640
I was helping you!

238
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:06,920
Are you crazy?

239
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,840
If Li Junsheng sees you,

240
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,160
he'll think we're together.

241
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,360
Wang Haotian isn't the killer.

242
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,280
Li Junsheng is.

243
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:20,880
You're in the loop too?

244
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,760
So you remember everything.

245
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,960
You remember it all, don't you?

246
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:55,160
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

247
00:11:57,080 --> 00:12:01,720
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

248
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,840
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

249
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,000
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

250
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:11,920
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

251
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:15,400
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

252
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:21,640
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

253
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:28,200
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

254
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,480
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

255
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:35,360
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

256
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,200
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

257
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:42,320
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

258
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,200
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

259
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:48,600
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

260
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

261
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

262
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:59,080
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

263
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:02,120
♪I could give you another future♪

264
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:08,560
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

265
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,880
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

266
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:12,520
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

267
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,280
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

268
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,560
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

269
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:20,560
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

270
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,520
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪

271
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:28,280
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪

272
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:34,720
♪I don't want an eternity without you♪

273
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:37,480
♪Even if holding on is more dangerous♪

274
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,160
♪More dangerous than letting go♪

275
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:42,360
♪At least we were real in this moment♪

276
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:46,040
♪At least none of this was pretend♪
